From eb2529231a3dfccf2bfe0c02b25947b267ad9a61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cory Forsythe <cory@coryforsythe.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:44:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/24] feat(bin): land the Hermes Agent (hermes CLI)
 crewmate/scout adapter

Detection (fm-hermes-lib.sh, mirroring the gemini node-bundle pattern for
hermes's python-venv shape), launch-then-send in fm-spawn.sh (--cli --yolo,
bare launch like kimi/rovo), a rendered-tail busy fallback in fm-busy-lib.sh,
and tmux/herdr liveness classification in fm-agent-process-lib.sh. hermes is
deliberately absent from fm-control-lib.sh: live verification found no safe
interrupt key (Ctrl+C exits the session, Escape does not cancel a running
tool call), so bin/fm-control.sh refuses hermes lifecycle actions rather than
guessing one.

Live-verified end to end through real bin/fm-spawn.sh against an isolated
scratch home and tmux server, including a delivery-gate fix discovered only
by driving a real dispatch: hermes's busy prompt row is not a composer shape
the shared classifier reads as empty, so delivery confirmation keys off the
submitted-message bullet instead of composer emptiness.

See docs/verification/hermes.md for the full evidence, including the
captain's terminal.backend: ssh config blocker reproduced live and left
undecided rather than silently forced around.
